# .gitattributes -- card #239's chantier, action A1 fix pass (F12).
#
# vendor/claude-agent-sdk/{sdk.mjs,package.json,LICENSE.md} are a third-party, minified vendor
# drop (see orchestrator/sdk.js's header and vendor/claude-agent-sdk/README.md for provenance) --
# nobody reviews a diff of sdk.mjs line-by-line, and `git diff`/`git log -p` doing so anyway is
# pure noise: it is a 1,556,674-byte, largely single-line file that would otherwise be diffed and
# language-classified like this repo's own hand-written code.
#
# `-diff` -- suppresses line-by-line diffing for this path (git shows "Binary files differ" or an
# equivalent instead); a real change still shows up as a changed file, just not expanded inline.
# `linguist-vendored` -- the GitHub Linguist convention (recognized by GitHub's own UI and by
# other tools that read .gitattributes for language stats) marking a path as vendored code, so it
# is excluded from the repo's language breakdown and from "changed files" review defaults that key
# off Linguist's vendored classification.
#
# Deliberately scoped to `vendor/**`, not the whole repo: this repo's own code should never get
# either treatment, and a future addition under `vendor/` (see doc/accepted-gaps.md §1's
# "Vendored or generated files" bucket) inherits this rule automatically without a second edit.
vendor/** -diff linguist-vendored

# Exception, added in this fix pass (R3): vendor/claude-agent-sdk/README.md is THIS repo's own
# prose, not a vendored third-party file (see that file's own top section, and F6/doc/
# remediation-plan-2026-08.md's execution rule 6, which puts it IN sibling-grep scope for exactly
# this reason). Git attributes apply last-match-wins within a file, so a later, more specific
# pattern overrides the blanket rule above for this one path. MEASURED (2026-09-17): without this
# line, `git check-attr diff -- vendor/claude-agent-sdk/README.md` read "unset" -- suppressing
# line-by-line diff on the one file in this directory that F6 explicitly declared reviewable, so a
# future correction to its md5/byte-count/version claims would have shown as "Binary files differ"
# instead of a real diff. `linguist-vendored` is left negated too, for the same reason: GitHub's
# language stats and "vendored" review defaults should see this file as ordinary repo prose.
vendor/**/README.md diff -linguist-vendored
